WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.367
-Our next guest hosts the new
series "B.S. The Game Show,"

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.167
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:08.234
He also returns as a judge
on the new season of

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:11.834
"America's Got Talent," which
premieres May 31st at 8:00 p.m.

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:13.367
right here on NBC.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:15.634
Please welcome Howie Mandel!

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:18.033
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:28.000
♪♪

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.501
Howie Mandel. That's what I'm
talking about. Wow.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:32.100
-My God.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.501
Wow. What a day.
-Oh, my God.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.667
-I got to just say.
I got here early.

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:38.400
And I got to meet Post Malone.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.734
He has been such
an influence on me.

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:44.701
[ Laughter ]
And just to spend quality time

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:47.167
with that guy, oh, my gosh.
-You're a big fan?

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:49.501
-Oh, I am. You have no idea.

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:51.234
-No, we have an idea.
I think we have an idea.

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:54.501
-No, you don't.
Post Malone means so much to me.

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:56.200
I adore him. And he is just --

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.000
People think, "How can he
influence you?"

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.100
And he does.
-He does.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.467
It's good to find out.
You learn something new.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.767
You look great.
How was the pandemic? Rough?

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:06.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:07.767
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.667
Yeah. I'll be honest with you.

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:12.100
I had COVID. I got COVID.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.601
-I can't believe
that you got COVID.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:17.634
-Because I go nowhere, I'm a
germophobe, but I won --

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:20.467
"A.G.T." won
the Kids' Choice Awards.

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:22.868
They made me go to
the Kids' Choice Awards.

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:25.901
And a lot of people get slimed.
I went viral.

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:28.701
[ Laughter ]
-Literally, yeah.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:32.634
-But I didn't feel -- I got
vaxxed and boosted, so I had

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:36.634
no -- The hardest thing for me
was to be locked in the room.

00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:38.467
I was locked --
I was quarantined.

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:40.901
-Of course, you have to.
-Yeah. I was.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:44.868
So I did the stick-and-poke, and
I figured that's what this is.

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:47.701
I did it to myself.
-You self-boostered.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:50.634
-I self-boostered myself.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:52.767
You know what was weird, though?

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:56.000
My wife, who takes lovely care
of me -- I love her.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.200
I've been married for 42 years.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.801
Said, "You got to quarantine for
10 days."

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:01.667
So for 10 days,
locked in a room.

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:03.534
Nobody. Did nothing. By myself.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:06.434
And then I got out, and I read
the CDC said five days.

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:07.968
My wife --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:10.701
It's not funny.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:10.701 --> 00:02:14.701
It's not funny.
-Yeah, alright, you're right.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.634
-Not funny.
You know what I realized?

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.067
We've been married 42 years.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:21.501
And I spent most of my life
on the road and traveling.

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:24.534
Up until COVID, I was doing
like 200 live dates a year.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:28.133
So the thrill was
not having me there.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:32.701
So the fact that I was there,
she imposed a quarantine.

00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:36.133
Every day, I would get up,
and I was going crazy.

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.000
But she locked me in the room,
and I could open the door

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.133
and there was a little cookie.

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:41.734
I played hide-and-go-seek alone.
Alone.

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:43.667
[ Laughter ]
-That's exciting.

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:46.834
Did you ever find yourself?
-Not -- Once. Once.

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:49.300
And it's because I used
the same hiding place twice.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:55.000
But just alone in the room going
"Ollie Ollie home free."

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.133
-I want to ask about -- I know
you have so many things

00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:01.200
going on, but one I really enjoy
is this podcast

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.267
that you kind of started with
your daughter.

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:04.100
-My daughter, Jacqueline Shultz.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.968
I do a podcast -- because I was
locked in at the beginning of

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:10.033
the pandemic and she wouldn't
come see me because I'm old.

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:11.734
And she thinks that --
No, because you weren't allowed

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.300
to be around people over 60.
-That's correct.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.033
-So she would phone me
and we would do prank calls.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:18.567
And we would spend hours.
And we'd do challenges.

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:19.901
And I'd call my friends.

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.968
And my wife came in and said,
"Why are you doing this?"

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.501
And I go,
"Just because it's fun."

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:25.767
And she said, "Record it."
So that became my podcast.

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:28.467
"Howie Mandel Does Stuff,"
and it's with my daughter.

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:30.601
[ Audience aws ]
Aww. Aww.

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:32.868
[ Laughter ]
This week, you know, Bill Burr,

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:35.434
Jim Jeffries --
Everybody comes by and does it.

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:37.534
And it's just -- Will you do it?

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:39.000
-Of course, I'll do it.
Yeah, I would love to.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.234
I'd do anything for
Howie Mandel.

00:03:40.234 --> 00:03:41.567
-Really?
-Yes.

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:42.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That is so great.

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:44.834
-Let's go get a tattoo after the
show. We'll talk about it.

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:47.734
-I will gladly
stick and poke you.

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:49.634
-Ah, thank you.
-If you're just tuning in,

00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:51.100
that doesn't sound right.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.734
-Yeah, but we were talking
about it earlier.

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:54.767
Let's talk about
"America's Got Talent" first.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.200
That's May 31st on NBC.
That's our big NBC show.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.834
-And we're all back.
-Everyone is back?

00:03:58.834 --> 00:04:01.434
-Everybody's back.
Simon is back.

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:03.634
Sofia is back. Heidi is back.

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:05.367
Terry Crews is back.

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:08.901
Simon is back on the bike,
which he shouldn't be.

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:10.534
-No.
-No.

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:12.567
-That was frightening enough.
-He's fallen off twice.

00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:14.167
-Twice?
-Twice.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.567
He broke his back.
He broke his arm.

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:20.334
He had a concussion,
and then he got engaged.

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:21.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:23.067
-You think there's a c--

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:24.667
-No, I don't think there's
a connection.

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.033
He's registered at Target

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:27.834
if anybody wants to get them
something.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:30.567
-Is he a Target guy?
-No, I was just joking.

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:32.300
-Oh good, yeah.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.601
Let's talk about "B.S."
-Okay.

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:35.334
-It's streaming right now
on Netflix.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.067
I can't say the actual title.
-No, you can't.

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:38.634
It's my favorite show
in the world.

00:04:38.634 --> 00:04:40.634
It really is because they said,
"Do a trivia show."

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:42.601
I said, "I hate trivia.
I know nothing."

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:45.868
But the key is, you don't have
to know the answers.

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:48.667
You just have to be able to tell
if the person is lying.

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:51.434
If you can lie, if you can B.S.
and convince one person

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:53.334
the answer is right,
you still win the money.

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:57.267
We gave away millions of dollars
to idiots who knew nothing.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:04:59.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes, finally.

00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:03.334
-That's on Netflix.
-Netflix said, "Yeah, perfect."

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:06.000
I like this idea for a show.
-It is.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.100
-It's fun.
-Do you B.S.?

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.067
-I could play.
Yeah, I could do, yeah.

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:11.501
I could probably win
a lot of money.

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:14.067
-Really? I think the best things
I've gotten in life is

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:15.767
because I B.S.'d because I lied.

00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:18.334
-Yeah, actually
I'm a terrible liar.

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:19.868
-Are you?
-I'm really bad.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.300
-I'm so good at lying.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.000
-But I'm good at trivia, so I
might be good at this game.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.000
-The trivia is real hard.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.300
You don't watch the show
for trivia.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.567
You watch the show to watch
their face like poker,

00:05:28.567 --> 00:05:32.100
to say, "This person knows
nothing. This is bull."

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.901
And if you can call them out --
If everybody calls bull

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:39.234
on the person and there actually
is bull, then they're out.

00:05:39.234 --> 00:05:42.033
But if they can convince one
person, they win the money.

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:43.601
-It's called
"B.S. The Game Show."

00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:48.033
-I wrote it right here.
-Here is Howie Mandel.

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:49.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:55.601
-I actually -- I took science,
and I...

00:05:55.601 --> 00:06:01.901
And I -- [Bleep] Sorry.
[ Laughs ] Um...

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:07.367
[ Laughs ]
Um...

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.300
No, the answer's bomboloni.
Sorry.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.868
I know that for a fact.

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:16.834
-And he took science.
-Yes, I took sci-- Well, yeah.

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:18.000
Bomboloni.

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:23.434
-He loves bomboloni,
and he took science.

00:06:23.434 --> 00:06:24.968
[ Applause ]

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:26.667
Was he lying? Was he bull?

00:06:26.667 --> 00:06:29.033
-That might be the worst liar.
-That was the worst.

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:30.667
-That was the worst liar.

00:06:30.667 --> 00:06:32.434
-I don't mean to say -- We can't
even say the name of the show.

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:33.767
I'm not allowed to say it.
Right?

00:06:33.767 --> 00:06:35.300
-You can say it.
We can't air it.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.300
But sure, say it.
-You know what?

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:38.567
And they even changed the name.

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:41.167
It wasn't always called "B.S."

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:43.033
-What was it called?
-"This [Bleep] Show."

00:06:43.033 --> 00:06:44.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:45.634
Howie Mandel, everybody.

00:06:45.634 --> 00:06:48.000
Check out "B.S." -- I'm happy
to do it with this one.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.634
"B.S. The Game Show"
now on Netflix.

